# CEO 2026-09-07 · R3 Sprint 1. reports/research/r3/ was ignored wholesale,
# which made the canonical R3 shadow ledger IMPOSSIBLE to accumulate: every
# CI run appended to a workspace that was then discarded, so a green
# pipeline run did not equal accumulated evidence. The ledger and the model
# artifacts are the R3 evidence base and must persist across runs.
# Everything else under r3/ stays ignored (scratch, intermediate frames).
reports/research/r3/*
!reports/research/r3/shadow_ledger.jsonl
# CEO 2026-09-09 · the evidence registry and the frozen-programme records
# are the governance answer to "which research branch is ready". Caught
# by the wildcard above they would be regenerated daily and never
# persisted - the same trap that hid the shadow ledger and lost the
# fundamental substrate outright.
!reports/research/r3/R3_EVIDENCE_REGISTRY.json
!reports/research/r3/R3_AI_MASTER_STATUS.json
!reports/research/r3/R3_AI_FINAL_SCORECARD.json
!reports/research/r3/R3_AI_DECISION_CONTRACT.json
!reports/research/r3/R3_AI_GOVERNANCE_AUDIT.json
!reports/research/r3/R3_AI_FREEZE_RECORD.json
# CEO 2026-09-08 · the R3_DECISION_v1 shadow ledger and its daily summary
# are the forward-evidence base: one append-only record per R2 candidate
# per day. They were caught by the wildcard above, so `git add` silently
# added nothing, the ledger never reached CI, and every R3 column in a
# CI-built workbook rendered NOT_EVALUATED. Excepted explicitly.
!reports/research/r3/shadow/
reports/research/r3/shadow/*
!reports/research/r3/shadow/*.jsonl
!reports/research/r3/shadow/*.json
!reports/research/r3/models/
reports/research/r3/models/*
!reports/research/r3/models/*.json
!reports/research/r3/models/*.pkl
